\@writefile{loc}{\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced~(rev): \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{we modify the MonofonIC transfer-function plugin above \(k_p\), rather than introducing a separately normalized curvature-spectrum amplitude. MonofonIC normalizes both PL and BT spectra to the same target \(\sigma _8=0.8111\), so the BT runs are not separate large-scale-amplitude fits. The resulting input linear matter power spectrum at \(z_i=200\) follows the broken-power-law enhancement described in Section~\ref {sec:theory}: the shape below \(k_p\) is the PL/Eisenstein shape up to the small global normalization factor, while the power at \(k>k_p\) is enhanced.}}{3}{section*.39}\protected@file@percent }
