\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces FOF halo mass functions for the PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep simulations at representative redshifts. Upper panels show the measured $dn/d\log _{10} M_{\rm  FOF}$ with Poisson error bars, together with the corresponding model-matched \replaced [id=rev]{Reed et al. (2007) FOF predictions}{Reed07 FOF predictions} evaluated with each \replaced [id=rev]{linear matter power spectrum generated from the PL or BT primordial power-spectrum template}{input linear power spectrum}. Lower panels show \replaced [id=rev]{BT\_soft/PL and BT\_deep/PL mass-function ratios}{the direct BT\_soft/PL and BT\_deep/PL mass-function ratios} in the same FOF mass bins. Here BT\_soft denotes the model with $k_p=1\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$ and $m_s=1.5$, while BT\_deep denotes the model with $k_p=10\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$ and $m_s=1.5$. All simulations use a $25\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}$ box with $1024^3$ particles. The gray band marks the interval between the nominal 20-particle halo threshold \(3.8\times 10^7\,M_\odot \) and the adopted plotted catalog cut \(M_{\rm  FOF}=10^8\,M_\odot \), roughly the 50-particle scale. The corresponding spherical-overdensity $M_{200c}$ comparison with \replaced [id=rev]{Bocquet et al. (2016)}{B16} is shown in Fig.~\ref {fig:m200c_bocquet16_hmf}.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
