\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Spherical-overdensity halo mass function comparison using \(M_{200c}\) masses and the \replaced [id=rev]{Bocquet et al. (2016) fitting function}{B16 fitting function}. Symbols show the measured SOAP \(M_{200c}\) mass functions for PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep, while lines show the corresponding \replaced [id=rev]{Bocquet et al. (2016) predictions}{B16 predictions} evaluated with each model's \replaced [id=rev]{linear matter power spectrum generated from the PL or BT primordial power-spectrum template}{input power spectrum}. The SOAP catalog cut is \(N_{\rm  DM}\ge 100\), and the plotted bins require \(M_{200c}\ge 2.0\times 10^8\,M_\odot \), close to the 100-particle scale \(1.9\times 10^8\,M_\odot \). The lower panels show \replaced [id=rev]{BT\_soft/PL and BT\_deep/PL mass-function ratios}{the direct BT\_soft/PL and BT\_deep/PL mass-function ratios} in the same \(M_{200c}\) bins.}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
